dropbearkey
Usage: dropbearkey -t ed25519 -f FILE

Make an ssh key.

	-t TYPE		key type -- ed25519 on xos (nothing else is built)
	-f FILE		where to write the private key
	-y		read a private key and print its public half

	dropbearkey -t ed25519 -f /state/id
	dropbearkey -y -f /state/id        # print the public key to hand out

The public half of titan's key goes in xos's authorized_keys, baked into
the read-only image; xos's own host key is made once, on the encrypted
state partition.

See also: dropbear, dbclient
